  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Spell checking
  </title>
  <p>
    Orca can present spelling errors and suggestions while you use a supported application's
    spell checker.
  </p>
  <p>
    Orca needs to identify the misspelled word, suggestions list, and other parts of the
    application's spell checker to present this information.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-spell-checking">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Spell Check</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Spell error</gui>: Controls whether Orca
          spells out the current error after speaking it. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Spell suggestion</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca spells out the current suggestion after speaking it. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present context of error</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca presents the surrounding text in which the mistake occurred. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
